From 3d4becfd01bfbd84458130138b9a18e075fdf7ad Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: permissionBRICK <40219477+permissionBRICK@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 17:38:22 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 21/24] usb: dwc3: qcom: wake a runtime-suspended controller on
 a plug-in (X1E80100)

A runtime-suspended controller on the Vivobook S 15 missed a device plugged
in: no PHY interrupt (dp/dm_hs_phy, ss_phy, pwr_event) arrived at all, so
runtime PM could only be used where something else reports the attach
(Type-C). This adds what the Windows driver stack of X1E80100 laptops does
before a controller leaves D0 (ACPI PEP tables and QcXhciFilter8380.sys), as
module parameters that are read at every runtime suspend.

On by default:
- runtime_sleep_clk: keep the "sleep" (suspend) clock on in runtime suspend
  (Windows D1/D2 keep gcc_usb30_*_sleep_clk on; only D3 turns it off).
  Turned off again for system suspend, so standby is unchanged. This is the
  fix: with it, plugging a stick into either USB-A port of the multiport
  controller raises dp_hs_phy_N and the device enumerates (tested on both
  ports, three times); without it nothing happens.
- wake_hold_ms=500: after a wakeup interrupt keep the xHCI host running for
  500 ms. xhci_resume() resumes the root hubs only if a port change is
  already latched (the 120 ms grace period applies only with suspended USB3
  devices) and xhci-hcd.N.auto (autosuspend delay 0) suspends again at once,
  so a connect that the controller had not latched yet was lost.
- eusb2_wake=-1 (auto: USB2 PHY compatible contains "eusb2"): with a device
  attached arm DM rising (HS/FS) or DP rising (LS) instead of DP/DM falling,
  as for eUSB2 repeaters (same as the pending upstream series "Modify
  interrupt handling for eUSB2 Phy targets" and the Windows driver tables).
  No change without a device (DP and DM rising).

Off by default (not needed for the plug-in wake; A/B tests via
/sys/module/dwc3_qcom/parameters/):
- runtime_pwr_event: request pwr_event / pwr_event_N and use it as a runtime
  wakeup source: PWR_EVNT_IRQ_MASK = LPM_OUT_L2 (+ POWERDOWN_OUT_P3 and
  LPM_OUT_RX_ELECIDLE for ports with a USB3 PHY), as the Windows filter
  programs 0xf885c/0xf89e0. Never a system wakeup source (GIC only).
- runtime_alt_irq: set QSCRATCH 0x20 bit 12 (+13 for the second MP port)
  after clearing 0x24, as the Windows filter does; meaning undocumented.
- icc_windows_bw: vote the usb-ddr bandwidth Windows votes in D0
  (0x28000000 B/s SS, 0x3938700 B/s HS, avg = peak) instead of
  1000/2500 MBps (SS) and 240/700 MBps (HS).

Not for upstream as is (module parameters, compatible-string check).
---
 drivers/usb/dwc3/dwc3-qcom.c | 465 +++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++----
 1 file changed, 418 insertions(+), 47 deletions(-)

